# default_pager manifest — the policy for the task that owns backing store
# (#511).
#
# 🔴 FOUND BY A CENSUS OF THE OTHER TARGET.  The permissive path was removed
# after counting what it served on x86-64, where the count reached zero.  This
# server does not run there.  On i386 it does, and it was refused a capability
# for its swap device the first boot after the removal:
#
#	(default_pager): cap_request('disk0c') FAILED: 2413
#	(default_pager): couldn't add device disk0c
#
# 🔑 A census is of one target, the same way a baseline is of one machine. The
# number was right and the conclusion drawn from it was not.

name default_pager

# RESOURCE_BLK_DEVICE (4), any device, READ|WRITE (0x3).
#
# ⚠️ `any' and not the hash of `disk0c'.  Which partition backs paging is an
# argument in bootstrap.conf -- argv[1] on this server's command line -- so a
# manifest that named one would be a policy about a configuration file rather
# than about this server.  What it may do is open a block device for reading
# and writing; WHICH one is decided by whoever configured the boot.
required 4 any 0x3
